                <pb facs="0620" n="532" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg532"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/1726: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-05-16T13:00:00-05:00">May 16, 1933—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>145. Lopez and party cordially received on arrival at 6 yesterday afternoon.
                    Press and public most evidently earnestly desire a settlement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
